 "form.rules": [
  "in a one-hand episode the resting arm's action columns = hold command = residual 0 (wrist Δ 0 · finger residual 0) — the recorded action is the ResidualArmIKAction residual (reference-based · trajectory-based), so finger target = lo + ½(clamp(base(reference) + residual·rs) + 1)·range · wrist target = reference wrist ⊕ residual Δ. When the resting arm's base is the rest pose (hand_surface.rest_finger_q · arm default pose — the base the bimanual resting hand idle_side uses), residual 0 yields that pose as it is. The record statement (action column term_modes) must name that term with both bases on, else it dies · the line action_fill names the source per side (recorded | hold_residual0)",
  "one hand × dataset = one form (collect_form) · missing columns = NaN · line absent_features (whole) · stats (stats_skip): a wholly absent column is left out of that episode's stats (LeRobot aggregate_stats gathers only the episodes that have the column) · actions are always filled (resting arm = hold command) → action stats = every episode"
 ],
